<h1>John Elleson</h1>
<p>US House, 9th District, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Party: Republican.</p>
<p><a href="https://johnelleson.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (johnelleson.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Elleson describes himself as a compassionate conservative and organizes his campaign around building trust, empowering families and bridging communities. His stances page says he favors aid-based programs for addiction, homelessness and mental health, removing regulations he calls burdensome to support small business, supporting law enforcement alongside de-escalation and community trust, and community-first health care with more local clinics. In his Sun-Times questionnaire he says he would restore pro-growth tax and regulatory policies and pursue energy independence, and names affordability and the cost of living as the district&#39;s top local issue.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Pastor of Lakewood Chapel in Arlington Heights with about 40 years in Chicago-area ministry, and the 2018 Republican nominee for this seat.</p>
